# FreeYFi Backend Rules

## Before coding
1. Read `y_fi_backend/.cursor/workflow/README.md` and relevant docs.
2. Check which clients use the endpoint: `y_fi`, `y_fi_partner`, `y_fi_frontend`.

## After coding (automatic — every turn, no user prompt)
1. Prepend to `.cursor/workflow/changelog.md` with `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM (UTC+6)`, files, why, API/DB impact.
2. Update `api-reference.md`, `database-flow.md`, or `business-logic.md` if contracts changed.
3. See `auto-changelog.mdc` — skipping this makes the task incomplete.

## Architecture
- Single Django app: `api/`. Logic in `api/view/*.py` + `api/serializer.py`.
- Do not add unused layers (services/repos) unless explicitly requested.
- JWT auth via `JWTAuthentication` on protected views. Partner group = lowercase `'partner'`.

## Financial constants
- Partner income: `total_income = round(total_ad_views × 0.34, 2)` — change only with client coordination.
- Session duration: clamp `[1, 10080]` minutes, default `30`.

## Multi-model review
Run parallel `/multi-model-review` before merging changes to: auth, income formula, ad tracking, ConnectedHistory sync, or migrations.

## Do not commit
- `.env`, credentials, `google-services.json` with secrets, keystore files.
